  "sourceFindings": [
    "Full selected entries 298–309 are retained in nine complete source chapters, 6–14. The chapter 7 introduction remains unchanged Arabic, separately browsable and excluded from sessions and narration scripts.",
    "The selected digital chain at 300 omits the feminine ending in that she said. Both inspected Arabic prints contain it. One declared correction restores only the missing letter; unchanged original wording, exact offsets, hashes and both witnesses remain accessible offline.",
    "The closing safflower-water observation at 303, the compiler’s alternate chain at 307, the final Prophet attribution, all repeated dialogue at 308 and the narrator’s alternative at 309 retain their original positions.",
    "Historical chain/reporting-verb differences and the rubbing-word variant at 306 remain documented without silently replacing the selected source.",
    "Cloth/perfume terms at 307, the cleansing material at 308, and the possible meanings of three times at 309 carry separate uncertainty notes with classical-commentary references. The notes are excluded from narration scripts.",
    "All twelve English comparison bodies were individually matched. EPUB 1.6.301–1.6.312 and Bewley 298–309 are comparisons, not proof of full-chain identity or independent certification.",
    "All 297 preceding entry objects and five other book packs remain unchanged. Actual audio bytes remain unchanged; no new recording was made."
  ],
